      <title>✖️ The Hustle This is how you order at Luckin Coffee: no line, no register. Just</title>
      <link>https://t.me/KissmeBabyFeedTwitter/24372</link>
      <description>&lt;div class="tgme_widget_message_text js-message_text" dir="auto"&gt;&lt;tg-emoji emoji-id="5355148941878900494"&gt;&lt;i class="emoji" style="background-image:url('//telegram.org/img/emoji/40/E29C96.png')"&gt;&lt;b&gt;✖️&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/tg-emoji&gt; &lt;a href="https://x.com/TheHustle/status/2116329939658231907" onclick="return confirm('Open this link?\n\n'+this.href);" rel="noopener" target="_blank"&gt;The Hustle&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;This is how you order at Luckin Coffee: no line, no register. Just a QR code, and your drink waiting for you on a shelf.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;In 2020, China had over 100,000 coffee shops competing for the same customers. Starbucks was the clear leader.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;But long lines and premium prices left a gap, and &lt;a href="https://twitter.com/luckincoffeeus" onclick="return confirm('Open this link?\n\n'+this.href);" rel="noopener" target="_blank"&gt;@luckincoffeeus&lt;/a&gt; saw it. The company wrote that China's coffee market was too expensive and inconvenient.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;So Luckin went 100% cashier-less.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Now it's bringing that model to the US. Luckin opened its first American store in 2025 and has 20 New York locations in just over a year.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Meanwhile, Starbucks announced in 2025 it was closing 80 to 90 of its US pickup locations, calling them "too transactional, not enough warmth."&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Starbucks said it needs more human connection. Luckin said, "Here's a QR code."&lt;/div&gt;</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://t.me/KissmeBabyFeedTwitter/24372</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:51:47 +0000</pubDate>
